{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1516284-spirit-worlds-and-the-mind","id":1516284,"title":"Spirit Worlds and the Mind","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-26T16:57:20-07:00","id":1516284,"title":"Spirit Worlds and the Mind","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wikipedia</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The <b>autonomic nervous system</b> (<b>ANS</b>), formerly referred to as the <b>vegetative nervous system</b>, is a division of the <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nervous_system\" target=\"_blank\">nervous system</a> that supplies <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Viscera\" target=\"_blank\">internal organs</a>, smooth muscle and glands.<sup><a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Autonomic_nervous_system#cite_note-Dorlands-1\" target=\"_blank\">[1]</a></sup> The autonomic nervous system is a control system that acts largely unconsciously and regulates bodily functions, such as the <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heart_rate\" target=\"_blank\">heart rate</a>, its force of contraction, <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Digestion\" target=\"_blank\">digestion</a>, <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Respiratory_rate\" target=\"_blank\">respiratory rate</a>, <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pupillary_dilation\" target=\"_blank\">pupillary response</a>, <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Micturition\" target=\"_blank\">urination</a>, and <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sexual_arousal\" target=\"_blank\">sexual arousal</a>.<sup><a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Autonomic_nervous_system#cite_note-Human_Physiology_-_Janig-2\" target=\"_blank\">[2]</a></sup> This system is the primary mechanism in control of the <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fight-or-flight_response\" target=\"_blank\">fight-or-flight response</a>.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course! I got myself so caught up on the psychological aspects of our consciousness and what makes us human that I forgot about our &quot;worm-brains&quot;! I forgot all those pieces of our &quot;minds&quot; that dont get Freudian-Jungian at all, but rather the parts the regulate all of the revulsive inside of our meatbags packages!<br /> <br /> Ok, so new plan: the &quot;Primal Wilds&quot; (I still need a better plan) will no longer represent the world of the Senses, but rather it will be all those parts of our nervous system that dont go into the &quot;soul&quot; of us, but rather keep our bodily functions independent of our childhood repressed sexual desires for our mothers/fathers. It's going to be the part of the Spirit World responsible for keeping the Material Plane &quot;Pulsating&quot;. As such, this is the one area that is NOT accessible via Astral Plane AT ALL. There will be some connections towards Realms of Emotions and Realms of Senses, but that's about it. Transitioning between the &quot;Psychological Umbra&quot; and the &quot;Physiological Umbra&quot; will be hard and use hard to find pathways.<br /> <br /> Thus, this &quot;Physiological Umbra&quot; would be more akin to the &quot;Gaia World&quot; of the Werebeasts from WoD.<br /> <br /> Another idea I had was to make all Spirit Worlds have &quot;Rainbow Bridges&quot;, which are the pathways connecting different realms and/or zones.<br /> <br /> Those &quot;Rainbow Bridges&quot; will confer an eternal Aurora visage on ALL spiritual skies, increasing the sense of wonder of alien-like nature of these worlds, and those will represent the synapses and the interactions between thoughts - for example, a Rainbow Bridge opening between the Astral Plane and the Underworld would represent a memory being remembered and coming to the conscious mind, while a Rainbow Bridge between the Feywild and Astral Plane would represent the conscious mind creating imagined fantasy scenarios/ideas, and a &quot;Dark Bridge&quot; between the Abyss and the Underworld could represent a dark memory being repressed in the confines of the subconscious mind for example.<br /> <br /> Spirits of each realm in this sense could literally be seem as &quot;God's thoughts&quot;. Demons escaping the Abyss would be like repressed Dark Thoughts trying to rage and escape from their cage (just as Freud described, repressed thoughts come back with a vengeance).<br /> <br /> So guys, please give some suggestions, ideas, imputs, criticism... Did anyone like it, hate it or what<br /> <br /> PS: sorry for the new thread, I dont know what happened in the original that is not posting my posts\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}